# `.claude/skills/` IS COMMITTED, and the rule that used to ignore it was wrong
# for how this repo is actually worked on (2026-10-08). It read: "kept on local
# disk, not part of the product repo." That assumed a laptop. The work happens in
# cloud containers that are rebuilt from the repository every session, so a skill
# on local disk is a skill that is gone next time — and the thirty-three already
# here survive only because they were committed BEFORE that line was added, which
# a gitignore cannot undo. The rule was therefore already false about two thirds
# of the directory it named, and silently dropped anything added after it.

# Blender output from scripts/blender_score_cube.py — regenerate in ~20s with
#   blender --background --python scripts/blender_score_cube.py
scripts/score_scene/cube.blend
scripts/score_scene/cube.blend1
scripts/score_scene/cube.png

# Marketing-kit media: upstream ships ~18 MB of rendered example frames and an
# explainer video. No skill reads them — they are a showcase for that project's
# own README — so they were not copied in, and this keeps them out if they ever
# are (2026-10-08).
.claude/marketing-kit/media/
